The perk system in ''Human Host'' (internally called '''Skills''') is divided into three trees corresponding to the three main play modes: '''Survive''', '''Craft''', and '''Fight'''. You earn perk points by leveling up (gaining XP from any activity in the matching category).

Every perk maps to a runtime '''factor multiplier''' (<code>_xxx_Factor</code>) on the player's <code>Char_Skills</code> component. The current game exposes '''23 factor fields''' (see below); most of which correspond to a leveled perk.

== Trees ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Tree !! Focus !! Internal set
|-
| '''Survive''' || Foraging, mining, food / water efficiency, movement || <code>All_Skills_Set._SurviveSkills</code>
|-
| '''Craft''' || Workbench output, resource yield, structure durability || <code>All_Skills_Set._CraftSkills</code>
|-
| '''Fight''' || Damage output, damage resistance, weapon-specific bonuses || <code>All_Skills_Set._FightSkills</code>
|}

== Factor catalog ==

The following table maps each in-game skill effect to the runtime factor it modifies. This is what mod authors patch when they add or amplify perks. Perk display names in-game may differ from the human-readable page titles used here; the factor field name is the authoritative identifier.

{| class="wikitable sortable"
! Factor field !! Effect
|-
| <code>_adrlinMeleeDmg_Factor</code>       || Adrenaline: melee damage bonus (low-HP trigger)
|-
| <code>_adrlinStaCost_Factor</code>        || Adrenaline: reduced stamina cost
|-
| <code>_adrlinWaterCost_Factor</code>      || Adrenaline: reduced water consumption
|-
| <code>_bareBluntHitDownProb_Factor</code> || Bare fists / blunt: knockdown chance
|-
| <code>_bladeHitProb_Factor</code>         || Blade weapons: hit / crit chance
|-
| <code>_bowDamage_Factor</code>            || Bow damage
|-
| <code>_bowDrop_Factor</code>              || Bow arrow drop (reduces gravity effect on arrows)
|-
| <code>_fireRecoil_Factor</code>           || Firearms: recoil reduction
|-
| <code>_fireSpread_Factor</code>           || Firearms: shot spread reduction
|-
| <code>_foodWaterDecrease_Factor</code>    || Reduces food + water depletion rate
|-
| <code>_gunDamage_Factor</code>            || Firearm damage
|-
| <code>_maxHP_Factor</code>                || Increases max health
|-
| <code>_maxStamina_Factor</code>           || Increases max stamina
|-
| <code>_meleeDamage_Factor</code>          || General melee damage
|-
| <code>_minerDmg_Factor</code>             || Mining damage per swing (faster ore extraction)
|-
| <code>_moraleDmg_Factor</code>            || Morale damage: used against NPC morale mechanic
|-
| <code>_repair_Factor</code>               || Repair efficiency at workbenches
|-
| <code>_silenceStepDmg_Factor</code>       || Silent step: bonus damage on backstab / first hit
|-
| <code>_silentStepReduce_Factor</code>     || Silent step: reduced footstep sound radius
|-
| <code>_softLandDmgReduce_Factor</code>    || Fall damage reduction
|-
| <code>_staminaRege_Factor</code>          || Stamina regeneration rate
|-
| <code>_stoneSkinDmgReduce_Factor</code>   || Stone Skin incoming-damage reduction
|-
| <code>_woodJackDmg_Factor</code>          || Wood-chopping damage per swing
|}

All factors live on <code>Char_Skills</code> in the <code>Creature</code> assembly.

== Respec ==

Perk points can be refunded at a workbench specific to your character (Early Access: exact respec UI is still evolving).

